# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Listed above but not tracked by Homebrew
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   alfred canva claude cleanshot google-chrome grammarly-desktop lightburn
#   notion obsidian rectangle-pro slack utm warp whatsapp
#
# These 14 apps were installed by hand into /Applications before Homebrew knew
# about them, so they do not appear in `brew list --cask` here. Two consequences:
#
#   * `brew bundle dump` cannot see them, so `./snapshot.sh --diff` reports each
#     one as a removal on every run. That drift is permanent and expected — do
#     not drop these lines when merging Brewfile.generated.
#   * On a rebuild `install.sh` exports HOMEBREW_CASK_OPTS=--adopt, so Homebrew
#     takes ownership of an app already at the destination instead of aborting.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT installed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# MDM-managed — reinstall through the corporate channel, not Homebrew:
#   Company Portal, Microsoft Defender, OneDrive, Microsoft 365 Copilot Shim
#
# No cask available:
#   Kindle — Mac App Store only. `mas` is not installed on this machine;
#   add `brew "mas"` + `mas "Kindle", id: 302584613` if you want it automated.
#
# Optional. This machine runs powerlevel10k but has NO Nerd Font installed
# anywhere, so some prompt glyphs cannot render. Uncomment on a rebuild:
